              <span class="faq-question-number mono-label">04</span>
              <span class="faq-question-text">How are passwords and sensitive credentials protected?</span>
              <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline>
                </svg>
              </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer-wrap">
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Clippy automatically respects standard concealed clipboard markers from 1Password, Bitwarden, KeePassXC, and Apple Passwords. Sensitive values are encrypted on-device with AES-256-GCM via the Apple Keychain, with automatic masking in previews.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </details>

          <!-- Item 5 -->
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary class="faq-question">
              <span class="faq-question-number mono-label">05</span>
              <span class="faq-question-text">Is Clippy free and open source?</span>
              <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline>
                </svg>
              </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer-wrap">
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Yes. Clippy is licensed under the permissive MIT license on GitHub. You can inspect the complete Swift source code, contribute features, or compile the Xcode project yourself.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="section-divider"></div>
  </main>

